$NetBSD$

Use GLib main loops and GTK4 application lifecycle signals.
Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted). wxWindows licence, like upstream.
Each nested loop owns its quit state; default-context wakeups and one-shot
idle sources are retained. GtkWindow activation uses the toplevel list model.
GTK4 selective native YieldFor explicitly fails before dispatch: GTK4 removed
GDK's global event handler. Unrestricted Yield remains functional.
https://docs.gtk.org/glib/struct.MainLoop.html
https://docs.gtk.org/gtk4/migrating-3to4.html

